Incorrect require path for MagicLink module after file rename: The require statement references 'magic-link' (kebab-case) but the actual file is still named 'MagicLink.js' (PascalCase). This PR renamed many files to kebab-case, but this file was not renamed - it remains as MagicLink.js. When this code executes, Node.js will throw a MODULE_NOT_FOUND error because the path './../../lib/magic-link/magic-link' does not exist. The correct path should be './../../lib/magic-link/MagicLink' to match the actual file. This will cause the entire members API to fail to initialize, breaking member authentication, signup, and magic link functionality across the application.
